   334→        <section class="section">
   335→            <h2>About the 2D Graphics Engine</h2>
   336→
   337→            <h3>What is this?</h3>
   338→            <p>
   339→                This is a <strong>2D graphics API</strong> similar to OpenGL, but focused on 2D rendering instead of 3D. Just like OpenGL provides functions for drawing triangles and applying textures in 3D space, this engine provides a complete API for 2D drawing operations.
   340→            </p>
   341→            <p>
   342→                It's a software renderer built from scratch in C++, implementing functionality found in production libraries like <strong>Skia</strong> (used by Chrome and Android), <strong>Cairo</strong> (used by GTK and Firefox), and the <strong>HTML5 Canvas API</strong>. You give it high-level drawing commands—"draw a rectangle," "fill a path with a gradient," "apply a matrix transformation"—and it produces the actual pixel colors on screen.
   343→            </p>
   344→            <p>
   345→                <strong>Key Features:</strong>
   346→            </p>
   347→            <ul style="line-height: 1.8; color: #555;">
   348→                <li><strong>Shape Drawing:</strong> Rectangles, polygons, paths with curves</li>
   349→                <li><strong>Transformations:</strong> 2D affine matrices (translate, rotate, scale) with CTM stack</li>
   350→                <li><strong>Shaders:</strong> Solid colors, linear/radial/sweep gradients, bitmap textures with tile modes</li>
   351→                <li><strong>Compositing:</strong> Porter-Duff blend modes (12 modes including src-over, xor, multiply)</li>
   352→                <li><strong>Path Rendering:</strong> Winding fill rule, Bezier curve tessellation</li>
   353→                <li><strong>Advanced Geometry:</strong> Triangle meshes, Coons patches, shader composition</li>
   354→            </ul>
   355→
   356→            <h3>Technologies Used</h3>
   357→            <ul style="line-height: 1.8; color: #555;">
   358→                <li><strong>C++17:</strong> Core rendering engine implementation with hand-optimized rasterization algorithms</li>
   359→                <li><strong>WebAssembly:</strong> Compiles C++ to bytecode that runs at near-native speed in the browser</li>
   360→                <li><strong>Emscripten:</strong> Toolchain for compiling C++ to WebAssembly and generating JavaScript bindings</li>
   361→                <li><strong>HTML5 Canvas API:</strong> Display target for the rendered pixel buffer (ARGB → RGBA at 60fps)</li>
   362→            </ul>
   363→
   364→            <h3>The Rendering Pipeline</h3>
   365→            <p>
   366→                Every draw call flows through this pipeline, transforming high-level commands into pixel colors:
   367→            </p>
   368→
   369→            <div class="pipeline-diagram">
   370→                <div class="pipeline-step">
   371→                    <h4>Draw Call</h4>
   372→                    <p>High-level command</p>
   373→                </div>
   374→                <div class="pipeline-arrow">→</div>
   375→                <div class="pipeline-step">
   376→                    <h4>Transform</h4>
   377→                    <p>Apply CTM matrix</p>
   378→                </div>
   379→                <div class="pipeline-arrow">→</div>
   380→                <div class="pipeline-step">
   381→                    <h4>Clip</h4>
   382→                    <p>Constrain to viewport</p>
   383→                </div>
   384→                <div class="pipeline-arrow">→</div>
   385→                <div class="pipeline-step">
   386→                    <h4>Rasterize</h4>
   387→                    <p>Edges to pixels</p>
   388→                </div>
   389→                <div class="pipeline-arrow">→</div>
   390→                <div class="pipeline-step">
   391→                    <h4>Shade</h4>
   392→                    <p>Compute color</p>
   393→                </div>
   394→                <div class="pipeline-arrow">→</div>
   395→                <div class="pipeline-step">
   396→                    <h4>Blend</h4>
   397→                    <p>Composite layers</p>
   398→                </div>
   399→                <div class="pipeline-arrow">→</div>
   400→                <div class="pipeline-step">
   401→                    <h4>Pixels</h4>
   402→                    <p>Final framebuffer</p>
   403→                </div>
   404→            </div>
